{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3455","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3455","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3455\",\"parent_revision\":\"6572c7e9976c7442a732cc639da23137e93335712fce6c6e424ab90526353cd2\",\"root_revision\":\"6572c7e9976c7442a732cc639da23137e93335712fce6c6e424ab90526353cd2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`sam_schema/core/backends/github_context_backend.py` contains a complete `ContextBackend` implementation \u2014 it stores active-task context as a sticky issue comment wrapped in `<!-- SAM:ACTIVE_TASK:{session_id} -->` markers (`:96,299-312`) and implements every protocol method.\\n\\nNothing can construct it. `create_context_backend` (`core/context_config.py:142-144`) raises before reaching it:\\n\\n    if resolved == \\\"github\\\":\\n        msg = \\\"GitHub context backend is implemented in T02. Use 'local' or 'memory' instead.\\\"\\n        raise NotImplementedError(msg)\\n\\n`\\\"github\\\"` is nonetheless a member of `_VALID_BACKENDS`, so it passes configuration validation and fails only at construction. A test asserts the raise (`tests/test_cli_active_task.py:129-140`), so the state is pinned rather than accidental.\\n\\n## Two further observations on the same class\\n\\n`list_active_tasks` on that backend returns only sessions present in an in-process `self._session_issues` dict (`:231-251`); a repo-wide marker scan is not implemented, so nothing survives a restart.\\n\\n`set_active_task` raises `ValueError` when `parent_issue_number` is None and `TypeError` on a beads nanoid (`:164-174`). A beads-tracked session therefore cannot be stored by this backend at all, independent of the factory.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nA configuration naming `github` for the context subsystem passes validation and then fails at first use. The failure text names a task ID \u2014 \\\"implemented in T02\\\" \u2014 from a plan that is not identified anywhere the reader can reach, so the message tells a user neither what to do nor what the state means.\\n\\nSeparately, a complete implementation sits unreachable in the tree. Anyone reading the backends directory sees four; three can be constructed.\\n\\n## Scope note\\n\\nEntangled with the open question of whether the active-task store survives at all \u2014 see #3431. If that store is removed, this file goes with it and the item closes rather than being fixed. Filed separately because the factory raising on a validated configuration value is a defect on its own terms, and because the shipped `T02` reference in a user-facing error is one regardless of the outcome.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA configuration naming `github` for the context subsystem passes validation and then fails at first use. The failure text names a task ID \u2014 \\\"implemented in T02\\\" \u2014 from a plan that is not identified anywhere the reader can reach, so the message tells a user neither what to do nor what the state means.\\n\\nSeparately, a complete implementation sits unreachable in the tree. Anyone reading the backends directory sees four; three can be constructed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session audit of the context backend surface, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Note\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEntangled with the open question of whether the active-task store survives at all \u2014 see #3431. If that store is removed, this file goes with it and the item closes rather than being fixed. Filed separately because the factory raising on a validated configuration value is a defect on its own terms, and because the shipped `T02` reference in a user-facing error is one regardless of the outcome.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Two Further Observations On The Same Class\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`list_active_tasks` on that backend returns only sessions present in an in-process `self._session_issues` dict (`:231-251`); a repo-wide marker scan is not implemented, so nothing survives a restart.\\n\\n`set_active_task` raises `ValueError` when `parent_issue_number` is None and `TypeError` on a beads nanoid (`:164-174`). A beads-tracked session therefore cannot be stored by this backend at all, independent of the factory.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2c11693ae9f948bd6e0febd80e63dd0fdb0ddd88b878c80ddb4628e8d5bcc68e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSAS_A\"}"}